OL,3,GNEWSAMinister warns people to save
OL,4,Awater amid drought
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe government is urging people to save
OL,7,Fwater as it warns action is needed to
OL,8,Fprevent severe drought conditions
OL,9,Fbecoming "the new normal".
OL,11,FWater and flooding minister Emma Hardy
OL,12,Ftold MPs current drought conditions "is
OL,13,Fsomething we have not experienced for
OL,14,Fdecades" and urged people to "think
OL,15,Fabout ways to use water wisely over the
OL,16,Fcoming weeks".
OL,18,FSevere drought was declared across
OL,19,Fparts of southern England on Thursday
OL,20,Fafter months of low rainfall, with
OL,21,Faround 50 million people now impacted.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,334,330,200,160,0,100
